{title: 04 Alabanzas sin cesar}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{lyricist: G; A; Sherwell}
{composer: John B. Dykes, 1861 (1823-1876)}

{sov}
[D]Alabanzas sin[A7] ce[D]sar ento[G]ne[A7]mos[D] al Se[A]ñor;
[D]himnos mil a[G] su[D] bon[A]dad[Em7] en[F#]to[Bm]nemos[G] con[A] a[Em7]mor[D][A7][D].
[D]Él nos da[G] la[D7] ple[G]ni[D]tud[G] de[Bm7] su[D] gracia ce[A7]les[D]tial[A];
[D]es la fuente[G] de[D] sa[A]lud[F#] pa[Bm]ra el[G] in[A]fe[Em]liz[D] mor[A7]tal[D].
{eov}

{sov}
[D]Del pecado abru[A7]ma[D]dor él nos[G] vino[A7] a[D] liber[A]tar;
[D]nos o[G]fre[D]ce[A] sal[Em7]va[F#]ción[Bm], y nos[G] lla[A]ma[Em7] sin ce[D]sar[A7][D].
[D]Ya pode[G]mos[D7] re[G]co[D]rrer[G] el[Bm7] ca[D]mino te[A7]rre[D]nal[A]
[D]sin temor[G] has[D]ta[A] obtener[F#] nues[Bm]tra[G] herencia[A] ce[Em]les[D]tial[A7][D].
{eov}

{sov}
[D]Y entretanto[A7] que[D] el Señor nos[G] re[A7]ciba[D] donde es[A]tá,
[D]entonemos[G] el[D] lo[A]or[Em7] que[F#] bon[Bm]dado[G]so[A] a[Em7]cepta[D]rá[A7][D].
[D]Mientras huelle[G] nuestro[D7] pie[G] es[D]te[G] mundo[Bm7] pe[D]cador[A7][D][A],
[D]ofrezcá[G]mos[D]le[A] con fe[F#] nues[Bm]tro[G] canto[A], nuestro[Em] amor[D][A7][D].
{eov}
